  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Security Rules**\n\nI\'ve successfully obtained the configuration and shifted focus to crafting `firestore.rules`. I\'m now cross-referencing the \"Payload-First Security TDD\" and \"Primitive Definition\" phases to ensure the security specification aligns with Firebase requirements. The initial task involves creating this `firestore.rules` file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Schema Entities**\n\nI\'ve examined the schema, focusing on `User` and `FoodLog` entities within the change logs and `firebase-blueprint.json`. I\'m now designing security rules for `/users/{userId}` and `/users/{userId}/logs/{logId}`. I\'m starting with `users/{userId}` and the `rules_version = \'2\'`. I\'m thinking about granting GET and CREATE/UPDATE permissions. I will leverage helper functions like `isValidUser(data)` and their corresponding checks, such as `data.userId == request.auth.uid`, `data.age is int && data.age >= 0 && data.age <= 120`, and more.\n\n\n**Refining Data Validation**\n\nI\'m now integrating validation rules into the `isValidUser(data)` function. I\'ve added checks for `weight`, `goal`, `targetCalories`, `targetProtein`, `targetCarbs`, and `targetFat`, ensuring they meet specified criteria. I\'m also examining the `isValidLog(data)` function for `/users/{userId}/logs/{logId}` to check for data types, `id`, `foodName`, and `mealType` to ensure that a log is valid. Now, I will implement read/write/update on the logs, to allow users to create and edit their own logs. I\'m taking another look at the user id to ensure it matches the request authorization.\n\n\n\n**Validating Log Entries**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `isValidLog(data)` function. I\'ve added a series of checks for `mealType` (ensuring it\'s one of a valid set), `calories`, `protein`, `carbs`, and `fat` (all positive integers). I\'m also including `ingredients` (a list with a size limit and string type check) and `imageUrl` (a string with a size limit). I\'m also ensuring the correct string format for `loggedAt` and `createdAt`. The emphasis now is on rule validation and correctness.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `security_spec.md` file detailing our security models, the \"Dirty Dozen\" adversarial payloads we must guard against, and the data invariant specifications to satisfy the critical security workflow."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 650704999
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
