ogic. I\'ve realized the `isValidId` function might be the problem. I\'m going to test changing the deletion rule to directly check the `logId` string length and type. I believe this will remove any regex complexities from Firestore rules and make deletion more robust. I\'m focusing on these changes: `allow delete: if isSignedIn() && request.auth.uid == userId && logId is string && logId.size() <= 128;`. This makes things much simpler.\n\n\n"
