lt-in dark mode capabilities in Tailwind v4 and confirming that the default configuration aligns with the plan. It appears Tailwind handles the `dark:` variant out-of-the-box, triggering on system preferences or a `.dark` class, which is perfect. I will now integrate this directly in to the document or `app-root` element. My current goal is now to confirm that I\'m able to apply a class to the `document.documentElement`, to leverage Tailwind\'s `dark:` variant and handle light/dark mode changes effectively.\n\n\n**Confirming Elegant Implementation**\n\nNow, I\'m thrilled with the simplicity! Applying the `dark` class directly to `document.documentElement` seems perfect for universal theming. I have a clean, elegant solution using a state variable, a `useEffect` hook, and local storage to manage and persist theme preferences. The Tailwind\'s `dark:` variant works like a charm! My current implementation now includes an example state update to `document.documentElement` in a `useEffect` hook. I think this approach is robust and will provide a flawless experience.\n\n\n**Locating Theme Toggle Placement**\n\nI\'m now determining where to integrate the theme toggle. I think the existing navigation bar in `DashboardView.tsx`, specifically the user info and logout button section, is an ideal spot. I\'m reviewing the current structure, focusing on lines 123-135, to identify the best placement within the UI for the new toggle.\n\n\n"
