      title: "tailwindcss.com"
    }
    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, the configuration for dark mode, especially when using a class selector for manual toggling, has shifted to a CSS-first approach, eliminating the need for a `tailwind.config.js` file for this purpose. You now define your dark mode class selector directly within your main CSS file using the `@custom-variant` directive.[1][2][3][4]\n\nTo enable dark mode based on a class (e.g., `.dark`) added to a parent element like `<html>` or `<body>`, you would add the following line to your CSS:\n\n\n\nSources:\n[1] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHgE_79D1Wovoa4etMClYTIGyBNggcdbuopl6QZtWTjJSQSKskD-kOIA0szTGX0JaM9nOUGj_9J6Zm-8KWPBt4lLkKTB-d53ILSWJhy_Sw78EuFZwxWHO863BfM9b1G9O9N0omX0nx_9WB8ztxLv4cFsyZ-)\n[2] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFk-PtswuYiQBgW02vb4_RmjLZOXSTSoJgsyloXv2Wjwwog0AAetjvbHXwzrOj5fyBwgeSKcDVHmPAfmEpwSm7EIvDPsciYhC6g_q5FaNsEtFldEj6hMmM2PdVx_-cuAp6FCgs8ufoXjeLqMiuKE9WLZJAGi-FJNd6DA4Pzz_n4DqsgRfeUEK9OY-VFfRUm1Ij8Iy7-tjpMIeR_6E3u9B_SogjInQ==)\n[3] [digitalapplied.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSpf0Raofas7qFiwV_9uhyfkEGFOk0n0wAdPL23B-ji-e2bcCUBQY9Rt_tUGPQXmzWh--e-pd3PEQyPqnQV8G66UuKY52P35aXw6U7vnxIuOTndpBcURknhabUE0x_uMumhWFmFc5hVC6sbrBSvAgiioflTDX9oEzUz1DAg7RnqhkgLyXx0F6RPTb2)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGojoyqJnHe6M_UKBIduQEIibTPB19fQAepq8yMV5OnieMULJLvhs2u6ubtZ_g8HU9De1Pqm8M2zDi3qoFxesoFHF3Ha33opWlWg0aF-47aelGIqZ-w9XSvXXHcl-oaTOKSEfBuT8DYsRHpqSlWotMH0AVXN3IoH30A72mw0Z0vIPd_laucKh2rBfKYFvFFmtjx7j61uclMxg==)\n[5] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGJhNG3GmNh2CbkgJr-5YfpIKvz7StLav9FqYklVHMJg3A8MaCF9vindcIwLF8yLWE0XvK1abgAxxGwh4eFOnUiq31s2T-R2dyBuhVVQCJ9_988-jgIzbN0ZHtAmVTPeSXuK5B8XAKJbH6U-ushKXxev3G5)\n[6] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQ