    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, the approach to implementing dark mode with a class selector has shifted to a CSS-first strategy, eliminating the need for `darkMode: \'class\'` in `tailwind.config.js`[1]. Instead, you define a custom dark variant directly within your CSS using the `@custom-variant` directive.\n\nTo enable dark mode via a class selector in Tailwind CSS v4, you would typically add the following to your CSS file:\n\n\n\nSources:\n[1] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEuJ9lI8Z2DPAd1Nmwjwlf70RjZRa9yXM2TGncQ27a45MSYS5rL0HCjmyHOnIAJiB7UZnVGCR8ifjW0JzmaKsxMGDerTB5ez7szBKMhdqQiS1pxUbTeznBNuGV0U8MUastncP5njU0zNVDGvCYGUMGOIay8)\n[2] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH0KhrMZ_fc2HeaZgxi8cjM8FQZIRa7SaE6GHFTfGNg3cLTPjTeRwLNubgaO8VwE9SJivI4bC7yDqtl79SAGDXIIWOYdw7P-S65XaoA3y79iQQIb8J3hQgLZkuC5W5Pxrmjksz87cNP8c3RASxqPCOG0vKK)\n[3] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEBqf5YDE9Q5Ruytx6qV4ADH3T7Va2MmwLT6yL5GJ7NeXAnzHeKMTqm9fVz66hhKwMIhOxA4-cgHM53uRiUgcKA-3qlzRTiAxWb0zIVRaGDKryfitGmoB3HiXP8J2iNQrq34jVjLs0=)\n[4] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGtJTfXzO5OqvOCl8fV6ZnwgLeMZePRB1BL4X3D-P12YxcruHYFeRhRXqqe2r3wthEuCo_PjrcqumE4V_zBIUK1X-ZDCdKwfw-iHisFcW7kHi9sBGNGgpO5WeQNtNdX2Al8wdCiMQA=)\n[5] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHpfFxr2IgSadgAMpzyg1AtJguL612rZVsUP_-u47xZnElkBD0S3JRw9iW4E_uWc_I-qRjfHkE5oX6tWHHzk7vW1agebuZxDGRrlLlA-6oWQWU2JdZC8Pzf51Bzgpnflh_RqiNr3aAgpRYd6fgVIGP6CrEh2xcEqYfz_wiSkG_BCgIK-orkUZNc-L2b6IdBK-sDvrC19QDRgyRzEz1n)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHbr8q1IGaxccFvfIl2aQhI6uPNcsWvIrGI7it9qFmpkAGNz9mzu20rrSFZ-eVmKMoWXuX9vhF8ToojlQXJidScettoDo_bYflW8w--CRX0iuL4vTBdHhHami9Z79MTKOVONmqMTaTd7Al3f70X2xDL-L_t0F95_wk=)\n[7] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.