    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFDR6_WBndAYiyBiCgq9wFbLnfPTO6URlm0q4wQkgGfucUHq3zgSa1Ci9N13jvP_jnnpR3RLa5eVsEYE-CsDmALyfWCjdf-Ei6Mh_0yatK-x88hKOvJrkRzfuXE-yyY9edPEQiFfZNYOfdmBN-MEDgl-qXy6ZbJ7kvYF82EWwG_t2IIEjKLMFX3sHGtZfRhTyK-_66gpTWpg8iU67ej0Pgu6n7cjxr4iw=="
      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "Tailwind CSS provides a flexible and efficient way to implement dark mode, primarily through its `dark:` variant and two main strategies: `media` and `class` (or `selector` in newer versions). For Tailwind CSS v4, there are specific approaches to defining and using custom dark variants.\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of implementing dark mode in Tailwind CSS:\n\n**1. The `dark:` Variant**\nThe core of Tailwind\'s dark mode functionality is the `dark:` variant. You can prepend `dark:` to any utility class to apply styles conditionally when dark mode is active. For example, `bg-white text-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-white` will set a white background and dark text in light mode, and a dark gray background with white text in dark mode. This keeps styles for both modes co-located with their respective elements, simplifying styling logic.[1][2][3][4]\n\n**2. Dark Mode Strategies**\n\nYou choose your preferred dark mode strategy in your `tailwind.config.js` file:\n\n*   **Media Strategy (Default)**\n    *   This strategy automatically applies dark mode styles based on the user\'s operating system preference, using the `prefers-color-scheme` CSS media query.[1][2][3][5][6]\n    *   It\'s enabled by default, so you don\'t need to configure `darkMode` in `tailwind.config.js` or you can explicitly set `darkMode: \'media\'`.[2][6]\n    *   No JavaScript is required for this approach.[6]\n    *   This is suitable for simple websites like blogs or documentation where manual toggling isn\'t needed.[6]\n\n*   **Class Strategy (Manual Toggling)**\n    *   This strategy allows users to manually toggle dark mode within your application.[1][2][3][5][6]\n    *   To enable it, set `darkMode: \'class\'` in your `tailwind.config.js` file.[2][6][7] (Note: In Tailwind CSS v3.4.1, the `class` strategy was replaced by `selector`[5]).\n    *   With this strategy, dark mode styles are applied whenever an ancestor element (typically the `<html>` tag) has the `.dark` class.[1][3][5][6]\n    *   You\'ll need JavaScript to add or remove the `.dark` class from the `<html>` element and to persist the user\'s preference (e.g., using `localStorage`) across page loads to prevent a \"flash of unstyled content\" (FOUC).[1][3][5][7]\n\n**3. `@variant dark` and Tailwind CSS v4**\n\nIn Tailwind CSS v4, dark mode implementation leverages the new CSS-first configuration system and CSS variables. While the `dark:` variant remains the method for applying conditional styles, the way you define the dark variant\'s behavior can change:\n\n*   **Defining a Custom Dark Variant**: You can define a custom `dark` variant in your main CSS file (e.g., `src/index.css` or `global.css`) using `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));` or `@variant dark (.dark &);`. This tells Tailwind to apply styles when a parent element has the `.dark` class.[8][9][10][11]\n*   **CSS Variable Overrides**: With the `@theme` directive in Tailwind v4, you can define base styles using CSS variables. For dark mode, you would typically override these CSS variable values within a `.dark` class, often within a `@layer theme` block in your CSS.[10][11] For example:\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [stevekinney.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJPQQUk2R2Xjw1ghN-f3nQDj10qvniUKlTsIQp9AsgeWJ_n1Qa-FgLXG1KrNctD-gbiWJEBfd-J6BIbYpk6fBSXnaIfSLLBcoARwVywcty-hKcWEjyuBPQwc3T2212YEQ-maBRa1EMWO76NIuE)\n[2] [tryhoverify.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFV6gilkNYkU2_CAEpPgk6Zw_DPemt-GGz3Z2vw27XSWX232HT9PmQ0RiwiSYKiMhnAJs1RjxEuQcfcQUw_wTxG3xEe562tjCGz4zQCqd93dT_z9FS8MkU08wjrtZwVoh7MoCQ_mFchRiV-E7jqRxapgv0mx7cZ1RDaX2F2M3TBYlb4Zt3tKkEA-NWSH8Q1)\n[3] [tailwindcss.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEFYOilQmPL64AXohBC4z8KlyhUUlmdQzRgLi14vMvmNJzRRAQNJy_5oeM_oCohJ4D-mxL3kDJqSri_11CNWG3UHz9-oojzYPa1VwaaHxgiBDsuWDNsxXfRVNr6_YdTach_)\n[4] [flowbite.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGkCiuyXgbpt25u0MgbN6Sn9u93tmth19Ja5I-bMHhpd9SDnogB5sYNHDsayaVNdLApvtqy-gX4ij2ktjRm9z9e_bPUWqzivt8dnpVkWrsr2svhJtebc3tZ5E7CzDwDOBKwswerOs-3tbA=)\n[5] [prismic.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH3HrT9otCZLe1wQjcp6N5XItIpcKHDjMz0_fh--MIvuxg3XL72fsI65uxEIsPZ4O3cF_jqgKmlarKlJJ439UofwtCoxTEFyXqOoqPRz5nPBNesG_PjuqnaoNPwG0KMxoqTr8zut6cFohYjsy5OLkTV2A==)\n[6] [magicui.design](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFPY2D9l3KbOXsj4LvIP_NSvHOwWtA-aGWsFPiXgAlrZTH-rO1gQl7h8eSl8PhnqoswmSVhiu4wcVtJC0dhfw3ALTKseCwNzXSDCjFVjyHKgGUh6sw2PNnrdcQxdm89Nvp8AUCCXhzZ5us=)\n[7] [cruip.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGIWrL66rZtY3F6JWGAcXGL7H3fTqqheE3ou2QOL_WEF2DN9Cut7abQXpJ3I2KZ27RPUcI70z6qmuaRjvKBK5LFeYQG7L83pbNFeWc5MpTwxMKRjaO9HrHytQGUNGQikeYptoZCyKwViaVHRta0iG_3Ul44FBOxlM8K1UH-ErUHw0RhRmAJvlNK)\n[8] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4o9bVvtTfgF9WLqaD_QFB8yvtxEDvVOqnyXhKdb1UQcq33KhZP3x4v4FsDmMlc1Hpv9Lu2GyV4GH0ATMUYOzwHRO0UDj7O5NHyGT0hYggox_5mdEXym9zjbNLdxQ7LZqnTjb7FT0=)\n[9] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSJj3w7sRPtzockEpH_iJc1Xhj8B_u6WtnkGJbEuSl-to8xeLpojWezQDKCkrsSEh8pk6ayqxRJnK_Ts5Nqno5p6BJaCJMehSE12JHiK06A8Nu7Z-c3eIhD71n0iFYYjZs_d4FmOq1YrUgg4nfDNN_sEro)\n[10] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQESTxqU0mHlVE9RyzAuEfTdUvjWrUhYpPwhymLqHGPxDUh8AFqn33L03VVuQowRio3Pqu-W-GJebrRFpQykQ0C04u4bqNoxr1ES2U2ovKGwzlLfUyq5Poa5R6Gptx4wTJzVWyT3EVXtEUwhEMBKqr1gGh_8yx9_6seC4ilGvyr1TsPulrHInKAx76kLdhdoFunYUrr3EFI1odreS6tjCeDcbey2cw==)\n[11] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFDR6_WBndAYiyBiCgq9wFbLnfPTO6URlm0q4wQkgGfucUHq3zgSa1Ci9N13jvP_jnnpR3RLa5eVsEYE-CsDmALyfWCjdf-Ei6Mh_0yatK-x88hKOvJrkRzfuXE-yyY9edPEQiFfZNYOfdmBN-MEDgl-qXy6ZbJ7kvYF82EWwG_t2IIEjKLMFX3sHGtZfRhTyK-_66gpTWpg8iU67ej0Pgu6n7cjxr4iw==)"
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
