          text: "Using variants to style your site in dark mode."
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 13
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Dark mode"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "[Overview](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#overview)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "[Toggling dark mode manually](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#toggling-dark-mode-manually)"
          }
          text: "## [Overview](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#overview)\n[Overview](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#overview)\nNow that dark mode is a first-class feature of many operating systems, it\'s becoming more and more common to design a dark version of your website to go along with the default design.\nTo make this as easy as possible, Tailwind includes a dark variant that lets you style your site differently when dark mode is enabled:\n\n```\ndark\n```\n\nLight mode\nWrites upside-down\nThe Zero Gravity Pen can be used to write in any orientation, including upside-down. It even works in outer space.\nDark mode\nWrites upside-down\nThe Zero Gravity Pen can be used to write in any orientation, including upside-down. It even works in outer space.\n\n```\n<div class=\"bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg px-6 py-8 ring shadow-xl ring-gray-900/5\"> <div> <span class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-indigo-500 p-2 shadow-lg\"> <svg class=\"h-6 w-6 stroke-white\" ...> <!-- ... --> </svg> </span> </div> <h3 class=\"text-gray-900 dark:text-white mt-5 text-base font-medium tracking-tight \">Writes upside-down</h3> <p class=\"text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm \"> The Zero Gravity Pen can be used to write in any orientation, including upside-down. It even works in outer space. </p></div>\n```\n\n\n```\n<div class=\"bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg px-6 py-8 ring shadow-xl ring-gray-900/5\"> <div> <span class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-indigo-500 p-2 shadow-lg\"> <svg class=\"h-6 w-6 stroke-white\" ...> <!-- ... --> </svg> </span> </div> <h3 class=\"text-gray-900 dark:text-white mt-5 text-base font-medium tracking-tight \">Writes upside-down</h3> <p class=\"text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm \"> The Zero Gravity Pen can be used to write in any orientation, including upside-down. It even works in outer space. </p></div>\n```\n\nBy default this uses the prefers-color-scheme CSS media feature, but you can also build sites that support [toggling dark mode manually](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#toggling-dark-mode-manually) by overriding the dark variant.\n\n```\nprefers-color-scheme\n```\n\n## [Toggling dark mode manually](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#toggling-dark-mode-manually)\n[Toggling dark mode manually](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ByqRpnmTA4PXz8OfgyT8ogWgtlVxzQTzC0xXc5fzP07_A-shkwtSCbM8Z2ZcUSI_i9Qss11FE35SFj6hZ3quS9h6GbZ_1IOOtw34weB0lYTzHPxuTHJ2rpI2fWJC2mzf#toggling-dark-mode-manually)\nIf you want your dark theme to be driven by a CSS selector instead of the prefers-color-scheme media query, override the dark variant to use your custom selector:\n\n```\nprefers-color-scheme\n```\n\n\n```\ndark\n```\n\n\n```\n@import \"tailwindcss\";@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));\n```\n\n\n```\n@import \"tailwindcss\";@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));\n```\n\nNow instead of dark:* utilities being applied based on prefers-color-scheme, they will be applied whenever the dark class is present earlier in the HTML tree:\n\n```\ndark:*\n```\n\n\n```\nprefers-color-scheme\n```\n\n\n```\ndark\n```\n\n\n```\n<html class=\"dark\"> <body> <div class=\"bg-white dark:bg-black\"> <!-- ... --> </div> </body></html>\n```\n\n\n```\n<html class=\"dark\"> <body> <div class=\"bg-white dark:bg-black\"> <!-- ... --> </div> </body></html>\n```\n\nHow you add the dark class to the html element is up to you, but a common approach is to use a bit of JavaScript that updates the class attribute and syncs that preference to somewhere like localStorage.\n\n```\ndark\n```\n\n\n```\nhtml\n```\n\n\n```\nclass\n```\n\n\n```\nlocalStorage\n```"
        }
      }
