      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "To manually toggle dark mode in Tailwind CSS v4, you can override the default `dark` variant to use a custom CSS selector instead of the `prefers-color-scheme` media query[1].\n\nHere\'s how to achieve this using the `@custom-variant` directive in your CSS:\n*   **Override the `dark` variant**: In your `app.css` file, you can define the `dark` variant to look for a `.dark` class (or any other custom selector) on the `html` element or any parent element. For instance:\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [tailwindcss.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEUqJ0VHvMtVPxP431W-6U_Psr-_b-JPDl-TWIz-HEz9YMhYstd1hcbKiM5gFtdR31gbj4pEXxT48BRbBtVhFdhXEkm3CeYhGsmBtYzzCLuh8kXDyzlOd5fTFyjfIbBlk5I)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGEkU4embdeNrseMgR72kHzkC7TghVsxANIZ18E_XtJTpOD-lJ8jMX86K486_h3QlS9yuy9hGqqLAT_DgrQoC5ZpW-FTQ0RBzH7OgpwDUhRMPqB-d_rR2eotv4rc91kSM07S2Q_aw8_IwCrlCR8-Qcg_g_7V5f6wlv-LGVhSeROMacWXPgC15pr_IZOO5bHpGqw)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHzjO-Elnu6ucaHckZikP4ywKT8JGUq-t1eXn4MGmjMdubuYir85TobetfVq4RpF9knlVIOuyRHFFpclWDaqnmWm40FR3yb96q_Tggxy9cIoCUAJ28eyuAdWmQP8-Ag1r0EIKGVwAlcUAmCC9yBJJUJkmVxqi6HYN3ec_HWfTOQ4bgCZzwqEmzpoyzSLxcC3bkgX8769B2OH7mRNGtTohLl4b9EPfBMf5Ok91yk-h4KP64-9hl93g==)"
