      title: "medium.com"
    }
    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, the `@variant dark` is configured directly within your CSS file using the `@custom-variant` directive. This allows you to define how the `dark:` prefix in your utility classes should behave, such as applying styles when a specific class (e.g., `.dark`) is present on a parent element, typically the `<html>` tag.[1][2][3]\n\nTo set up a class-based dark mode, you would add a line similar to the following in your main CSS file (e.g., `input.css` or `global.css`):\n\n\n\nSources:\n[1] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrSWomdgcImBjbiy-pbTZhyPYdiRYefozDYJVnEEkEhtk6fLeZ5W62vf6kJWWQCoy9BYCh5YmcWwvtYwGMqxEYg6gpkwfpySxcFkG6A4aDOCdAlkKL0NXGuxqdCcsdD-X1LtkYQqI0CXLcU3fq1GjSRi_f)\n[2] [kitemetric.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGTLUbw3wol6O_uGivkQ7jZstRKAmghJ-MQmzzljG31MPtvaoG_Qj6xWTB7AAjkUc2SzySQFhbTzvHVQBGdCSf7ptq8pN11sgmQMv_l7T3iSiZpxY7bFFdrkihe5ptM4U9j5Bs-PFDU9-EEt000Hnke6bTdmfMUyacW9rCVYzCYNRYVIztkVRI1yZqohX6G5EiIhMOM)\n[3] [tailwindcss.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEtnzd8ANM9_vGrjo_zTO1Srvh87SAmu3ZZpwZyMSNQUTJsKPJwpMAp6sUHU7SPmLs1rn7oQ3cKeb9z38p8L_yyRDM7Lyo8Ps-_-A1kz7f9ruxUOpNORnOHwxZT3URa_n0Y)\n[4] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEY8OPi9ew7E5P4QWKpAqJLKPywHUn7Nmrxj3t8eXDzi73ca29VZ9WrBTXKph3iIM4kD5MIWIxEFf0Z74Oalgkzavg9lyrKuUspPG3bCSX5ugpE6UBrFukytApcVUc3Qd9Vwaf-spw=)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHBrVP8LhXNt1kSTITmG8y4agW8WQWuzc9HM9ld-wj203Ghkoh0Cn-QvCn3Uz6UXvtvZA27OCtfolt2gTneb1f90iu-SCm1E1Jno3ZPmhNa9ckYpErxAomOShfPMTjgUr-eew81wv5RDNpyWOF1O-oLB9QoiPZxWTYs4V_SHs58MJMk1r96S8z1teWtXVHfj74ppmEt0atQi0WOSh6MNAD8YW9o8Q==)"
