o match. I\'ve also updated the text and icon colors to reflect these changes and create a cohesive style.\n\n\n**Evaluating Style Inheritance**\n\nMy current focus is on the profile card\'s structure and styling within the broader component ecosystem. I\'m examining its inheritance model, its reliance on specific color classes, and the impact of the classes across light and dark modes. I\'m noting the `bg-slate-50`, `dark:bg-slate-950/40`, and border classes, to determine best practices.\n\n\n**Refining Card Element Styling**\n\nI am now closely inspecting the visual presentation of the profile cards and the reset button. I\'m focusing on aligning the font sizes, colors, and overall appearance of these components, particularly in the context of light and dark mode transitions. I need to be sure the styles are easily maintainable.\n\n\n**Confirming Code Alignment**\n\nI\'ve just successfully implemented the visual updates and replaced the code in `DashboardView.tsx`, ensuring that Bento Card 3 now fully reflects the unified styling consistent with Cards 1 and 2. I\'ve reconfirmed the light and dark mode states and hover states are all consistent. The change is in at line 300, and fully complete.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Interactions**\n\nI\'m now examining the integration of the user profile statistics (weight, height, age) and the rest of the profile card. I see the stats inherit a similar style, with `bg-slate-850`, `dark:bg-slate-950/40`, and border properties. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent styling for all related components. I\'m also ensuring the text is correctly colored.\n\n\n"
