    modified_response: "To test your application directly on your phone, you can utilize the public live URLs. Since the app is hosted securely on Cloud Run, it is fully accessible from any mobile browser with an active internet connection.\n\nHere is how you can set it up and run your tests:\n\n### 1. Accessing the App on Your Phone\nChoose one of the active environment URLs depending on your testing intent:\n*   **Shared App (Recommended)**: Use this for the stable, production-ready snapshot of your application.\n    *   **URL**: `https://ais-pre-34dds7x722tcefrgzlxtbx-573898277506.us-west2.run.app`\n*   **Development App**: Use this if you are actively editing the code and want to see your changes refresh live.\n    *   **URL**: `https://ais-dev-34dds7x722tcefrgzlxtbx-573898277506.us-west2.run.app`\n\n### 2. Quick Ways to Open the Link\n*   **QR Code Method (Fastest)**: Open a QR code generator website (or search \"QR generator\" in your desktop browser), paste the link, and scan the generated QR code using your phone\'s native camera.\n*   **Message/Email**: Send the link to yourself via email, Slack, WhatsApp, or any other messaging client.\n\n### 3. Key Mobile Features to Test\nOnce you open the link on your mobile browser (such as Safari on iOS or Chrome on Android) and sign in, you can test the native mobile integrations:\n*   **Full Camera Capture**: Tap the camera or upload icons in the **Meal Logger**. Because it is accessed over HTTPS, your browser will prompt you for camera permissions, allowing you to take pictures of food directly with your phone\'s camera!\n*   **Responsive Layout**: Check the biometric settings card, charts, and logging inputs. They have been styled with responsive tailwind utility classes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) to fit naturally on compact screens.\n*   **Dynamic Data Sync**: When you log a meal from your phone, watch your dashboard on your desktop web browser update instantly thanks to real-time sync with Google Firestore!"
