  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Tracking Personal Progress**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s need to track their personal project\'s progress. They want to test on their phone, but I\'m holding off on specific answers to deployment and testing until I have a clearer picture of their priorities. Right now, it\'s about helping them monitor their own work.\n\n\n**Clarifying Personal Usage**\n\nI\'ve realized the user\'s focus is personal access and testing, not public deployment. They mentioned running it on their phone and tracking progress. I\'m prioritizing providing direct access methods. Using the Shared App URL or Development App URL in their phone\'s browser, as this is a mobile-responsive web app. I\'ll explain how they can easily add it to their home screen for simple access.\n\n\n**Highlighting Immediate Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the user can immediately access their app. I\'m emphasizing that the Shared App URL is already a live, hosted web application on Google Cloud Run, perfect for mobile access. I will explain that adding it to their phone\'s home screen is all it takes for continuous progress tracking. I\'m creating a clear and encouraging response.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Since this is a personal project to track your own progress, you are already in a fantastic position! Because Google AI Studio Build hosts your application on a live cloud container, you do not need to pay for hosting or set up complex pipelines to use it on your phone or in daily life. \n\nHere is exactly how you can start using it on your phone and run/host it long-term:\n\n---\n\n### 1. How to Run and Test It on Your Phone Right Now\nYour app is fully mobile-responsive and optimized for touch interactions. You can access it instantly:\n1. **Open your phone\'s web browser** (Safari on iOS, Chrome on Android).\n2. **Enter your Shared App URL**: \n   `https://ais-pre-34dds7x722tcefrgzlxtbx-573898277506.us-west2.run.app`\n3. **Log in or Sign up**: The application uses actual Firebase Authentication and a secure Firestore database. Any meals you log, goals you set, or biometrics you update on your phone will save in real-time and synchronize if you open the app on your computer.\n\n#### \360\237\222\241 Tip: Add it to your Home Screen (Like an App)\nTo make it feel like a real native app:\n* **On iPhone (Safari)**: Tap the **Share** button (box with an up arrow) at the bottom, scroll down, and tap **Add to Home Screen**.\n* **On Android (Chrome)**: Tap the **three dots menu** in the top right and select **Add to Home screen** or **Install app**.\nThis places a neat launcher icon on your phone\'s home screen, hiding the browser address bar for a full-screen, native application experience.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Is it already \"Published\" in Real Life?\n**Yes!** The **Shared App URL** (`ais-pre-...`) is a production-ready, active, and securely hosted URL running on Google Cloud Run. \n* As long as you keep your AI Studio project active, you can use this URL indefinitely to track your historical progress, log your real meals via camera or upload, and manage your biometrics.\n* The backend is wired to your dedicated, secure Firebase Firestore database, ensuring that only you (via your authenticated login) can write and read your data.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Export and Host it Independently (Optional)\nIf you ever want to move the project out of AI Studio to have full ownership under your own domain name or hosting account, the process is straightforward:\n\n1. **Export the Code**:\n   * Click on the settings/export menu icon in the top-right corner of the AI Studio workspace.\n   * You can download the entire projekt as a **ZIP file** or **Export to GitHub**.\n2. **Deploying the Frontend (Free)**:\n   * Since the frontend is a standard React + Vite application, you can upload your repository to free static hosting providers like **Vercel**, **Netlify**, or **GitHub Pages**.\n3. **Your Database**:\n   * The app is designed using standard client-side Firebase SDK integration. If you want to run it completely on your own, you would just create a free personal Firebase project on the [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/), copy your new configuration keys to replace the current ones, and deploy the rules.\n\nFor now, bookmark your **Shared App URL** on your phone, add it to your home screen, and start tracking your everyday biometric progress and nutrition logs! Let me know if you need any adjustments to the existing features as you begin testing it."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 187302299
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
